// @emit-error print of a nullable literal union — narrow it first
// CONTRACT (must-error): `print(v)` over an UN-NARROWED `K | null` niche. `exprIsLitAtom`
// claims such a binding on the standing assumption that a consuming position has already
// narrowed it non-null, and it takes the member texts from the NARROWED type — so an
// un-narrowed one has NO member texts and master emitted an EMPTY widening chain: rc=0 and
// NO OUTPUT for a local or a param, the quietest possible wrong answer. (The same program
// written with a module GLOBAL instead built a module that failed to parse as WebAssembly.)
//
// There is no member text for the null arm to print, so the rule is the one the nullable
// STRING beside it already carries: narrow it first. The narrowed spelling runs —
// `print-narrowed-nullable-litunion.vl`.

type K = "a" | "b"

function show(v: K | null) { print(v) }

show("a")
